            <ArticleTitle>Symptomatic right ventricular ischemia secondary to a critical stenosis in a nondominant right coronary artery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>68-72</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/ccd.23482</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Stable angina pectoris owing to isolated right ventricular ischemia from a critical stenosis in a nondominant right coronary artery is a rare entity and documentation of isolated right ventricular ischemia even rarer. We present a case of isolated right ventricular ischemia documented by fractional flow reserve (FFR) and resolution of symptoms after percutaneous coronary intervention.</AbstractText>
